\hyaHzee

01:22.180 --> 01:28.260
www.saizen-fansubs.com

01:22.180 --> 01:28.260
#saizen@irc.rizon.net

01:33.050 --> 01:34.820
The second half's started.

01:34.820 --> 01:37.380
So Tsubasa can't play.

01:37.380 --> 01:41.260
They're without Tsubasa. They won't have any goals at the end of this half!

01:41.260 --> 01:43.540
What?! Damn it!

01:48.020 --> 01:51.300
Forget it. However mortifying, it's a total defeat.

01:51.300 --> 01:54.020
Tsubasa, you're free to laugh.

01:54.020 --> 01:56.180
These are our real capabilities.

01:56.180 --> 01:58.260
The game's not over yet!

01:58.260 --> 02:01.340
We'll give it our all until the final whistle blows!

02:01.820 --> 02:04.660
This is what the Japanese Junior Youth spirit is all about!

02:07.380 --> 02:09.300
Go for it, Hyuga-kun!

02:09.300 --> 02:10.820
Here I go!

02:11.840 --> 02:14.300
Uh-oh! He's now one-on-one with the keeper!

02:14.300 --> 02:16.020
Take this!

02:21.510 --> 02:22.910
You ran away.

02:22.910 --> 02:25.900
And here I was thinking you were gonna fire a long shot.

02:25.900 --> 02:27.390
You bastard!

02:27.390 --> 02:28.620
Calm down, Hyuga!

02:28.620 --> 02:30.160
Enough of this.

02:30.160 --> 02:34.700
Consider this goal as a present from me, since you came all the way from Japan.

02:35.230 --> 02:41.900
But with this coward as your captain, you'll never win a single game in France!

02:42.430 --> 02:44.550
Stop it, Hyuga.

02:44.550 --> 02:45.900
Let go of me!

02:45.900 --> 02:47.340
Hyuga-kun!

03:00.130 --> 03:01.430
Hyuga-kun...

03:07.380 --> 03:12.540
<b>The Glorious Number 10</b>

03:07.380 --> 03:12.540
<b>The Glorious Number 10</b>

03:31.520 --> 03:32.940
I'll be leaving.

03:32.940 --> 03:34.060
All right.

03:34.060 --> 03:38.740
We, the Japanese delegation, just got our butts handed to us by the Germans.

03:38.760 --> 03:42.360
What's worse is that Tsubasa was here to see it.

03:42.900 --> 03:44.620
Yeah...

03:45.100 --> 03:50.620
He came all the way to Germany, yet he wasn't able to play.

03:50.620 --> 03:54.100
I wonder what the coach was thinking?

03:58.880 --> 04:04.100
If Tsubasa was playing, those guys would never take us for jokes!

04:17.370 --> 04:18.100
Roberto...

04:18.850 --> 04:21.320
I came to Europe.

04:21.320 --> 04:25.290
Even if we all speak different 
languages, soccer is a world sport.

04:27.190 --> 04:30.340
I wanna hurry and play against the international players!

04:32.630 --> 04:33.480
Tsubasa!

04:33.480 --> 04:34.340
Eh?

04:35.140 --> 04:36.770
Wakabayashi-kun!

04:36.770 --> 04:38.340
Why are you here?

04:39.090 --> 04:42.030
Right back at you. What are <i>you</i> doing here?

04:42.030 --> 04:45.800
Don't you have a game against the Italian team today?

04:45.800 --> 04:48.860
I haven't been submitted as a member yet.

04:48.860 --> 04:52.780
The coach still wants me to watch my shoulder.

04:55.380 --> 05:00.690
He's still not letting you play even 
after that defeat against Grunwald?

05:01.390 --> 05:03.860
You can't underestimate Europeans like that.

05:04.340 --> 05:07.860
All Hyuga-kun and Matsuyama-kun have to do is find their place.

05:08.400 --> 05:10.090
We'll be fine today.

05:10.660 --> 05:11.620
You really think so?

05:11.620 --> 05:12.810
Eh?

05:17.460 --> 05:20.620
He's Zino Hernandez of the Italian team.

05:20.620 --> 05:24.940
They say he's the standout goal keeper from Italy.

05:25.620 --> 05:27.620
He's well known throughout Europe.

05:29.110 --> 05:31.100
Zino Hernandez, eh?

05:31.740 --> 05:33.580
The world is so vast.

05:34.090 --> 05:36.620
Schneider, Hernandez...

05:36.620 --> 05:40.120
There are so many amazing 
players I still don't know about.

05:41.260 --> 05:44.700
I want to play against them as soon as possible!

05:48.260 --> 05:49.100
Tsubasa.

05:50.260 --> 05:51.680
Let's go down.

05:51.680 --> 05:51.980
Sure.

05:56.830 --> 05:59.100
No way we're losing again.

06:00.410 --> 06:02.530
So they're the Italians, huh?

06:02.530 --> 06:04.620
They look strong.

06:06.570 --> 06:08.620
Wakabayashi!

06:08.620 --> 06:10.040
Wakabayashi!

06:11.200 --> 06:14.150
From this day forward, I'll be joining the Japanese team.

06:15.020 --> 06:19.660
I'll be representing the Japanese team during the tournament in France.

06:19.660 --> 06:21.420
I'll be counting on you.

06:21.420 --> 06:22.660
What?!

06:25.070 --> 06:26.080
Where's the coach?

06:26.080 --> 06:28.940
The Italian team called him over to discuss the game.

06:28.940 --> 06:32.650
Then, Misugi, I'm asking you as a coach...

06:32.650 --> 06:34.820
Why isn't Tsubasa playing?

06:34.820 --> 06:36.290
That's because...

06:37.150 --> 06:38.820
The coach decided it.

06:38.820 --> 06:44.460
And we can't always be 
dependent upon Tsubasa.

06:44.460 --> 06:46.820
You're being naïve, Matsuyama.

06:46.820 --> 06:51.420
All the teams watched the game against Grunwald.

06:51.420 --> 06:52.340
Them too!

06:54.700 --> 06:57.800
They seem to be laughing at us.

06:58.540 --> 07:03.980
You've surely been told that international soccer is a lot harder than you think!

07:04.570 --> 07:07.720
You have to give it your all. If not, you won't break down any walls!

07:13.390 --> 07:14.410
Misugi!

07:15.020 --> 07:16.390
Misugi...

07:17.130 --> 07:18.700
There's been a problem.

07:21.440 --> 07:23.000
I wonder what's happening.

07:23.570 --> 07:24.540
Could it be...

07:26.020 --> 07:28.860
Come over to the bench, everyone.

07:32.880 --> 07:35.360
We're going back, boys.

07:36.510 --> 07:39.340
The Italian team has refused to play this game.

07:39.800 --> 07:41.080
What?

07:41.080 --> 07:42.340
Why won't they?

07:42.340 --> 07:45.140
They watched our game against Grunwald.

07:45.140 --> 07:50.670
They believe that there's nothing to gain playing against the Japanese team.

07:50.670 --> 07:52.180
We're going back!

07:52.180 --> 07:53.890
What?!

07:55.020 --> 07:56.420
Damn!

07:56.420 --> 07:58.420
They're taking us for fools!

08:03.430 --> 08:05.410
Nothing to gain?!

08:09.210 --> 08:13.460
They'd rather rest up for the French tournament, I'll bet!

08:14.270 --> 08:17.080
They aren't taking us seriously!

08:17.080 --> 08:17.900
Damn it!

08:27.190 --> 08:28.140
Tsubasa!

08:28.140 --> 08:31.020
Here I come, Italian Junior Youth Team!

08:32.540 --> 08:34.680
Don't take us for jokes!

08:34.680 --> 08:35.700
Here I come!

08:36.550 --> 08:38.420
Try and stop me!

08:39.180 --> 08:41.020
Someone take him on.

08:41.020 --> 08:42.710
With pleasure.

08:42.710 --> 08:44.220
I'm going.

08:44.220 --> 08:47.820
Go get him, Conti! Show the Japanese Juniors what soccer's all about!

08:52.410 --> 08:54.660
You think you can win against us in soccer?

08:55.980 --> 08:57.580
He dribbled past me!

08:57.580 --> 08:59.340
He got around Conti!

08:59.340 --> 09:01.660
That's it, Tsubasa! Go! Go!

09:01.660 --> 09:04.540
I'm game! Let's get him!

09:18.300 --> 09:21.300
Tsubasa! Pass 'em, pass 'em!

09:28.410 --> 09:29.180
He did it!

09:31.540 --> 09:32.380
Go!

09:53.490 --> 09:56.950
He made it! That was his Drive Shot!

09:56.950 --> 09:59.020
Did you see that, Italy?!

10:00.290 --> 10:02.020
Tsubasa...

10:02.970 --> 10:07.370
Not only did he dribble past me, but he completely iced Hernandez.

10:07.820 --> 10:10.890
Japan has such a player?

10:10.890 --> 10:14.480
You're a genius, Tsubasa!

10:15.030 --> 10:16.580
Tsubasa!

10:16.580 --> 10:20.820
Tsubasa, your Drive Shot's really amazing!

10:22.530 --> 10:23.470
What happened?

10:23.470 --> 10:25.860
That wasn't like you, Hernandez.

10:27.560 --> 10:29.860
The Drive Shot, huh?

10:32.530 --> 10:34.860
It's time to go, everyone.

10:36.290 --> 10:38.300
And with your Drive Shot!

10:38.300 --> 10:39.920
That was too cool!

10:47.760 --> 10:49.480
His name's Tsubasa?

10:49.480 --> 10:51.020
I'll remember that.

10:51.920 --> 10:56.150
If Tsubasa comes back and we're all able to play soccer together again,

10:56.150 --> 10:58.420
we'll beat them for sure!

10:58.420 --> 11:03.340
Yeah! That's why he absolutely has to play in the next game.

11:03.340 --> 11:07.540
If Tsubasa plays, we'll be able to show 
what our team's really made of, Misugi!

11:07.550 --> 11:08.460
They're right!

11:09.900 --> 11:11.510
Tsubasa-kun,

11:11.510 --> 11:13.820
how's your shoulder feeling?

11:13.820 --> 11:17.890
Did you see what he did out there? Of course he's all right!

11:17.890 --> 11:19.580
I'm okay to go any time.

11:20.380 --> 11:21.820
Did you hear that, Misugi?

11:22.430 --> 11:24.820
Understood. I'll talk with the coach.

11:25.920 --> 11:28.540
We'll be able to show our true abilities on the pitch.

11:29.640 --> 11:36.300
In other words, the Japanese team can't 
show off its true skills without you, Tsubasa.

11:36.300 --> 11:37.870
Hyuga-kun.

11:42.500 --> 11:47.780
Germany - Roteburg Stadium

11:47.790 --> 11:49.380
I'll begin the introductions.

11:49.380 --> 11:56.370
I'm sure you all know Grunwald's ace striker 
and member of the German Junior Youth team,

11:56.370 --> 11:58.390
Karl Heinz Schneider.

11:58.390 --> 12:04.460
Schneider will be Roteburg's striker starting next season.

12:05.270 --> 12:06.420
Pleased to meet you.

12:06.420 --> 12:12.510
Now our opponent for this practice 
match came a long way from Japan.

12:12.510 --> 12:14.380
Greet them with respect.

12:14.380 --> 12:18.900
I heard that the team from Italy 
canceled their game against them.

12:19.370 --> 12:24.900
Since they're this far from home, let's show them what European soccer's really like.

12:24.900 --> 12:27.900
Yeah, and what soccer's all about, period.

12:28.540 --> 12:32.140
I think you'd better not underestimate Japan.

12:33.060 --> 12:37.630
On my Grunwald team, there's a Japanese goalkeeper who's far from being bad.

12:37.630 --> 12:40.780
It doesn't matter which country a soccer player comes from.

12:40.780 --> 12:44.140
If they're able to compete against us...

12:46.140 --> 12:47.940
...you cannot deny their skills!

13:04.700 --> 13:05.740
Schneider!

13:07.120 --> 13:07.660
Yo!

13:08.160 --> 13:09.420
What are you doing here?

13:09.420 --> 13:12.320
I went to say hello to the Roteburg team.

13:12.320 --> 13:14.190
Actually, that's an excuse.

13:14.190 --> 13:17.180
Today, I'll see what they're really worth.

13:18.120 --> 13:19.380
He will play, won't he?

13:19.380 --> 13:22.840
The one you consider a prodigy?

13:22.840 --> 13:23.180
He will.

13:24.370 --> 13:26.320
Ohzora Tsubasa. {NOTE: ALL INSTANCES FROM EP 13 ON NEED TO HAVE THIS NAME AS IT'S WRITTEN THIS CLEAR AS THE DAY ON THE STARTING LINEUP AT 13:29 IN EP 22}

13:30.900 --> 13:32.090
Let's go, Takeshi.

13:32.090 --> 13:32.980
Yeah!

13:34.390 --> 13:35.540
Good luck.

13:35.540 --> 13:36.650
Thanks.

13:36.650 --> 13:39.790
Tsubasa, what's this? You're still not changed?

13:39.790 --> 13:42.180
Hurry up, we're leaving ahead of you.

13:42.180 --> 13:43.940
Yeah, I'll be there soon.

13:59.740 --> 14:03.690
I finally get to wear my Japanese team uniform!

14:08.140 --> 14:11.940
There's no way I'm giving up 
wearing this Japanese uniform!

14:27.610 --> 14:31.340
I haven't played a game for a while. I've even changed position.

14:31.340 --> 14:35.900
Matsuyama-kun has been put back as a 
defender, and they made me the midfielder.

14:37.380 --> 14:39.840
I have a lot on my shoulders!

14:43.610 --> 14:48.020
It's the second game for the Japanese team with them kicking it off!

14:49.210 --> 14:51.570
How will Roteburg fare in this match?

14:53.980 --> 14:55.650
Don't let up for a second!

14:55.650 --> 14:56.580
Let's get 'em!

15:00.330 --> 15:03.240
Number 10 avoided their tackle!

15:03.780 --> 15:04.620
All right!

15:05.580 --> 15:06.900
Here I come!

15:06.900 --> 15:08.140
Tsubasa-san!

15:16.670 --> 15:17.940
Sawada!

15:19.660 --> 15:21.430
With Tsubasa-san's speed...

15:24.300 --> 15:27.820
Wakabayashi! Is this really the same team as before?

15:29.230 --> 15:30.820
They're just getting warmed up. {there's plenty more to come}

15:30.820 --> 15:31.820
Hyuga-kun!

15:32.980 --> 15:34.020
Now's the chance!

15:34.650 --> 15:35.900
They fell for it.

15:37.900 --> 15:39.460
It's an offside trap!

15:42.980 --> 15:44.860
Tsubasa, here!

15:46.570 --> 15:47.540
All right!

15:48.290 --> 15:49.660
Drive Shot!

15:49.940 --> 15:50.180
What?!

15:50.180 --> 15:51.300
A shot?!

15:51.300 --> 15:54.380
He's taking an unwise shot at the goal from that distance!

15:58.200 --> 16:00.300
W-What? A goal!

16:00.300 --> 16:02.410
What was that shot?

16:02.410 --> 16:04.020
I-Impossible.

16:04.020 --> 16:05.940
T-The ball just dropped in.

16:05.940 --> 16:09.260
T-T-Tsubasa!

16:09.750 --> 16:12.280
Japan's Number 10 scored the game's first goal!

16:12.280 --> 16:15.780
What a shocker! Japan made a goal from that distance!

16:16.710 --> 16:21.610
The game's barely begun, and Japan's already scored.

16:22.300 --> 16:23.660
Well done, Tsubasa.

16:24.190 --> 16:25.570
Matsuyama-kun.

16:25.570 --> 16:26.570
Tsubasa.

16:28.380 --> 16:30.120
Nice shot.

16:30.120 --> 16:31.100
Hyuga-kun...

16:32.970 --> 16:34.500
What do you think, Schneider?

16:35.860 --> 16:38.980
With this one goal, the team's 
mood has changed completely.

16:38.980 --> 16:42.500
That's Number 10 of the Japanese team, Ohzora Tsubasa.

16:46.660 --> 16:49.460
Roteburg is now trailing by one goal.

16:49.460 --> 16:51.770
Damn it! We let down our guard!

16:51.770 --> 16:54.230
That one goal was a freebie!

16:55.180 --> 16:56.460
Let's go!

16:56.460 --> 16:58.020
They won't be getting any more easy goals!

17:02.970 --> 17:05.860
Roteburg is now storming in on the attack!

17:05.860 --> 17:07.540
This is nothing like a few moments ago!

17:12.110 --> 17:13.550
He's coming full speed!

17:13.550 --> 17:14.460
Stop him!

17:14.460 --> 17:17.060
Roteburg now has a chance to shoot and score!

17:17.060 --> 17:18.180
I won't let you!

17:22.740 --> 17:23.460
Oh crap!

17:28.200 --> 17:29.930
Nice save, Wakashimazu!

17:29.930 --> 17:31.380
This one's for you, Tsubasa!

17:31.380 --> 17:32.420
It's the Number 10!

17:32.420 --> 17:34.060
Don't let him shoot!

17:34.060 --> 17:35.020
Hyuga-kun...

17:35.020 --> 17:36.260
Here I go!

17:37.260 --> 17:39.140
Nice pass, Tsubasa!

17:39.140 --> 17:40.660
Put it in, Hyuga-kun!

17:41.250 --> 17:42.500
This one's mine!

17:46.330 --> 17:49.340
It's in! What power and speed!

17:49.340 --> 17:51.340
It's a line drive goal!

17:51.340 --> 17:55.050
All right! We've scored two goals! Incredible!

17:55.050 --> 17:56.000
He did it!

17:56.000 --> 17:56.620
Hyuga-san!

17:57.250 --> 17:59.990
Tsubasa's not the only Japanese scoring threat.

17:59.990 --> 18:03.660
That shot by player Hyuga Kojirou was a thing of beauty!

18:03.660 --> 18:05.140
Well done!

18:06.620 --> 18:07.860
Tsubasa!

18:08.420 --> 18:12.900
So the Japanese team has changed this much just because they have Tsubasa?

18:12.900 --> 18:15.660
Even the shot from Number 9 was different than before.

18:16.900 --> 18:19.880
He's even improved the mood of the team.

18:19.880 --> 18:22.220
That's Ohzora Tsubasa for you.

18:23.550 --> 18:28.220
Ever since he entered, the team 
became more united and effective.

18:34.260 --> 18:36.900
All right! My hand's fine!

18:37.390 --> 18:39.020
Don't let up!

18:39.020 --> 18:40.020
Yeah!

18:42.900 --> 18:43.790
Yes!

18:43.790 --> 18:45.100
Leave it to me!

18:45.100 --> 18:46.510
Coach...

18:48.210 --> 18:52.100
So, this team will definitely become a roadblock for my ambitions

18:52.830 --> 18:55.580
to dominate the International Junior Youth Tournament.

18:58.610 --> 19:02.140
Ohzora Tsubasa of the Japanese Junior Youth team...

19:02.620 --> 19:03.620
What's wrong,

19:04.120 --> 19:05.200
Schneider?

19:05.820 --> 19:06.620
Nothing.

19:07.220 --> 19:09.140
You want to go up against this team?

19:09.140 --> 19:10.420
I do.

19:12.010 --> 19:13.020
I really do!

19:13.660 --> 19:16.500
The Japanese team's going at it. And Ohzora passes...

19:17.710 --> 19:18.700
...to Matsuyama!

19:24.270 --> 19:26.890
And he scores!

19:26.890 --> 19:27.620
Tsubasa!

19:31.620 --> 19:33.140
And that's the end of the game!

19:33.140 --> 19:34.620
3-0!

19:33.140 --> 19:34.620
We did it!

19:34.620 --> 19:37.620
FC Roteburg has lost against Japan.

19:38.630 --> 19:41.140
Their first win of the European Tour!

19:41.140 --> 19:45.090
And it's a total victory against 
Roteburg, with the score of 3-0!

19:45.090 --> 19:48.380
It was a magnificient game from the Japanese Junior Youth team!

19:54.180 --> 19:56.430
All right! We did it!

19:58.700 --> 20:02.620
Sign: Commercial Street of Nankatsu

20:02.620 --> 20:04.460
<b>Grocery Store</b>

20:08.830 --> 20:10.820
Not yet, Uncle?

20:10.820 --> 20:12.600
Hold on, hold on, I'm almost there.

20:12.600 --> 20:14.410
Are you sure you're fine?

20:14.410 --> 20:16.980
I'm telling you I am...

20:16.980 --> 20:18.260
Here it is!

20:19.770 --> 20:20.900
Where, where?

20:20.900 --> 20:22.500
I see him, I see him!

20:22.500 --> 20:29.360
They lost their first game in the tour against Grunwald, but they crushed Roteburg.

20:29.990 --> 20:31.800
Hey, Uncle!

20:31.800 --> 20:33.320
Are you listening, Uncle?

20:33.320 --> 20:33.980
Y-Y-Yeah.

20:34.460 --> 20:39.500
The Japanese Junior Youth team will be in France playing against other international Junior Teams.

20:39.500 --> 20:42.240
It means they're at their peak!

20:43.890 --> 20:44.980
There's even a photo!

20:46.090 --> 20:49.020
It's Tsubasa-kun! There's a picture of Tsubasa-kun!

20:49.020 --> 20:51.100
Uh? Which picture?

20:51.100 --> 20:52.300
Where is he?

20:52.780 --> 20:55.510
Aren't you glad, Sanae-chan?

20:55.510 --> 20:56.740
Auntie!

20:56.740 --> 21:01.620
Your beloved Tsubasa-kun is looking really good!

21:01.620 --> 21:03.730
But Sanae-chan...

21:03.730 --> 21:07.620
This picture's so small that we don't know who's who...

21:08.180 --> 21:10.370
You're so stupid.

21:10.370 --> 21:14.000
When you love someone, you'll see him clearly, no matter the size of the picture.

21:14.000 --> 21:14.660
Right?

21:14.660 --> 21:16.520
Auntie...

21:16.520 --> 21:18.270
Is that how it is?

21:22.140 --> 21:25.560
It looks like Tsubasa-kun and the others are going strong.

21:25.560 --> 21:27.660
That's good.

21:31.320 --> 21:33.540
Next up is France, Tsubasa-kun.

21:33.540 --> 21:35.140
You'll be able to see Misaki-kun.

21:45.170 --> 21:47.770
France, eh? Roberto...

21:47.770 --> 21:51.380
I'm going to France to be part of the the Junior Youth tournament.

21:52.040 --> 21:57.040
We'll finally be able to play against other international players.

21:57.040 --> 21:59.720
Watch us play soccer!

22:03.300 --> 22:09.340
Preview

22:04.440 --> 22:07.980
We, the Japanese team, have gone to France.

22:07.980 --> 22:11.900
For us, it's our first international game of the Junior Youth Championship in France.

22:11.900 --> 22:14.660
My heart races just thinking about it!

22:15.480 --> 22:18.980
Also, we reunited with our friend, Misaki-kun, after three years.

22:18.980 --> 22:22.890
All right, let's go! We're the "Golden Duo" of Japan!

22:22.890 --> 22:26.220
Next time, on Captain Tsubasa: The Golden Duo Reunites

22:24.300 --> 22:33.220
The Golden Duo Reunites

22:26.220 --> 22:27.300
Look forward to it!

22:27.300 --> 22:30.020
Let's aim for tomorrow! Get goal!

22:33.660 --> 22:37.500
tsumiageru jibun no takasa wa

22:33.660 --> 22:37.500
My skill keeps on growing.

22:37.500 --> 22:41.820
dare ni mo kimerarenai

22:37.500 --> 22:41.820
Nobody can measure it.

22:41.820 --> 22:45.500
komiageru jibun no yowasa wo

22:41.820 --> 22:45.500
The weakness that grows inside me,

22:45.500 --> 22:49.860
dare ni mo miserarenai

22:45.500 --> 22:49.860
I can't let anyone see it.

22:49.860 --> 22:57.780
aa tada maketakunai sono kimochi de

22:49.860 --> 22:57.780
Ah. It's just, I feel like I never want to lose...

22:57.780 --> 23:03.860
aa ima susumu yo

22:57.780 --> 23:03.860
Ah. Right now, I'll move forward.

23:09.740 --> 23:13.540
tondekuru koishi wo haratte

23:09.740 --> 23:13.540
I ward off the pebble flying towards me,

23:13.540 --> 23:17.860
bai no hayasa de kaesu

23:13.540 --> 23:17.860
And return it with twice as much speed.

23:17.860 --> 23:21.540
yandeiru kotori wo hirotte

23:17.860 --> 23:21.540
I pick up an ill little bird,

23:21.540 --> 23:25.900
ooki na sora ni kaesu

23:21.540 --> 23:25.900
and return it to the wide open sky.

23:25.900 --> 23:33.820
aa tada maketakunai sono kimochi de

23:25.900 --> 23:33.820
Ah. It's just, I feel like I never want to lose...

23:33.820 --> 23:39.820
aa ima susumu yo

23:33.820 --> 23:39.820
Ah. Right now, I'll move forward.

23:45.300 --> 23:49.860
ima daseru subete no chikara de

23:45.300 --> 23:49.860
Using all the strength I have,

23:49.860 --> 23:53.380
koukai wa shitakunai

23:49.860 --> 23:53.380
without feelings of regret...

23:53.380 --> 24:00.860
ima daseru subete no chikara de saikou no kachi

23:53.380 --> 24:00.860
Using all the strength I have, to the ultimate victory.
